implementationPlan.description:
Separate positively identified candidate refusals from environmental failures without parsing npm stderr or fabricating a check-job observation. Add the host prerequisite's exact constant DEPENDENCIES_CANDIDATE_INVALID = 82 beside DEPENDENCIES_FAILED = 81. Use a small dedicated exception type for candidate validation, distinct from ValueError/OSError and never carrying candidate data. Keep install_dependencies' boolean success/infra result for existing callers; its candidate-specific checks raise only the dedicated exception. At check_job's dependency call:
```py
try:
    if os.path.lexists(dependencies_manifest) and not install_dependencies(
            workspace, dependencies, toolchain, env, spawn, install_timeout):
        return DEPENDENCIES_FAILED
except CandidateDependencyInvalid:
    return DEPENDENCIES_CANDIDATE_INVALID
```
CandidateDependencyInvalid is NEW; choose this exact local class name and define it before the installer. Reuse 5ed445ca's manifest reader/comparison: distinguish reading/validating the protected lock and dependency-list/cache inputs (infra) from invalid candidate package metadata (candidate). Candidate package absent/not regular, invalid UTF8/JSON/shape/size, mismatch against valid approved root or forbidden overrides/bundling, and existing shrinkwrap/.npmrc guards are candidate causes. Unexpected OSError, access failure, corrupted approved lock, cache metadata, and all unclassified run_install failures stay infra. Error handling: distinguish ENOENT for the candidate manifest from I/O errors; never turn a generic exception or all False returns into code-failure. Preserve all-directories preflight, close fds, existing timeout/signal/GUARD cleanup, no-follow reads, no raw path/content logging and no-manifest behavior. No network or npm-output heuristic. No check command or relay starts on 82, and no hello/output/observation frame is emitted. Update supervisor's exit-code comments to explain 81 versus 82. C2 must now pin both Python and JS constants. Keep patch small and table-driven; no repair-policy production change.
